{"identifier":"SanFrancisco1955CinemascopeFilm","title":"San Francisco (1955 Cinemascope film)","description":"Cinemascope homage to the city of San Francisco made by amateur filmmaker and inventor Tullio Pellegrini.","videoUrl":"https://archive.org/download/SanFrancisco1955CinemascopeFilm/SanFrancisco.mp4","thumbnailUrl":"https://archive.org/services/img/SanFrancisco1955CinemascopeFilm","sourcePageUrl":"https://archive.org/details/SanFrancisco1955CinemascopeFilm","durationMs":1265000,"level":"C2","topic":"san francisco; amateur film; widescreen; Cinemascope, pasta1","sourceCredit":"Source: Internet Archive — San Francisco (1955 Cinemascope film)","hasCaptions":true,"segments":[{"startMs":18000,"endMs":24001,"text":"San Francisco, within its 45 square miles, has contained one of the most colorful and romantic cities in the world."},{"startMs":25001,"endMs":36001,"text":"Approaching from the south, the traveler views with sudden excitement the city trusting its white towers into the blue California sky. But it is"},{"startMs":36001,"endMs":42000,"text":"from the east that the city reveals its famous profile framed by the silver towers of the Bay Bridge."},{"startMs":65000,"endMs":81000,"text":"Seen from the north, the distant city crowns the tip of the peninsula that reaches into the broad waters of the surrounding bay. The gigantic portals of the"},{"startMs":81000,"endMs":94001,"text":"mighty bridge that spans the Golden Gate provide a dramatic entry. From the"},{"startMs":94001,"endMs":102000,"text":"outskirts, let us now move directly into the very heart of the city. The city"},{"startMs":102000,"endMs":121000,"text":"hall dominates the square which is flanked by the main public library, the state building, and the civic auditorium. Behind the city hall lie the veterans"},{"startMs":121000,"endMs":135000,"text":"building and the war credited with having stopped the onslaught of the 1906 fire,"},{"startMs":135001,"endMs":140000,"text":"Vanis Avenue still remains one of San Francisco's broadest thoroughfares."},{"startMs":157000,"endMs":168000,"text":"San Francisco is a city of many hills and Telegraph Hill is perhaps the most famous. Here was located the lookout station of early days. A semaphore from"},{"startMs":168000,"endMs":177001,"text":"which the hill derived its name signaled to ships approaching through the Golden Gate. A mecca for tourists, the hill provides a magnificent view of the bay and"},{"startMs":177001,"endMs":184001,"text":"its man-made wonders. Eight and a half miles in length,"},{"startMs":185000,"endMs":196001,"text":"the Bay Bridge is the longest bridge in the world. It is actually a two unit span divided in the middle by Yerba Buena Island. To the left of Yerba"},{"startMs":196001,"endMs":206001,"text":"Buena lies man-made Treasure Island, site of the 1939 World's Fair. Ships from the four corners of the earth find their way to San Francisco's Embarcadero."},{"startMs":210000,"endMs":215000,"text":"Famous for its infamous residence, Alcatraz Prison, Aelius the Rock."},{"startMs":218000,"endMs":224001,"text":"Stretching across the gateway to the Orient is the longest single span in the world, the mighty Golden Gate Bridge."},{"startMs":228000,"endMs":233001,"text":"At the foot of the hill lies colorful fisherman's wharf."},{"startMs":244000,"endMs":249000,"text":"Reminiscent of a Mediterranean scene, the wharf captures a bit of sunny Italy."},{"startMs":254001,"endMs":258000,"text":"Quaint seafood grattles and fine restaurants invite the gourmet."},{"startMs":263000,"endMs":276001,"text":"Typical of the wharf are the steaming petals of the sidewalk crab stands. The supply of fresh fish"},{"startMs":276001,"endMs":282000,"text":"and seafood is brought in daily by sturdy little craft that birthed the lagoon behind the restaurants."},{"startMs":326000,"endMs":337000,"text":"Between fishermen's wharf and the Golden Gate Bridge lies the fashionable Marina District with its handsome yacht harbor. This is the Marina District of today,"},{"startMs":337001,"endMs":345000,"text":"but perhaps this old photograph will remind old timers that this was the site of the 1915 Panama Pacific International Exposition."},{"startMs":348000,"endMs":355000,"text":"An architectural gem, the crumbling"},{"startMs":355000,"endMs":369000,"text":"Palace of Fine Arts is the only exposition building remaining today. Driving along the northern end of the peninsula, we reach the salient"},{"startMs":369000,"endMs":372000,"text":"point that provides the closest view of the Golden Gate Bridge."},{"startMs":401000,"endMs":421000,"text":"The California Palace of the Legion of Honor, one of San Francisco's finest museums, is an exact replica of the Legion of Honor in Paris. The one ski resort"},{"startMs":421000,"endMs":429001,"text":"of the 90s is now a"},{"startMs":435000,"endMs":440000,"text":"ride on the newly installed sky tram should be included in the tourist itinerary."},{"startMs":483000,"endMs":486000,"text":"Just below the cliff house is a year-round amusement park."},{"startMs":519001,"endMs":553001,"text":"My miles of picturesque motor roads lead us through the largest man-made park in"},{"startMs":553001,"endMs":564000,"text":"the world. Created out of a wilderness of shifting sand dunes, over 1,000 acres of verdant meadows, shady lanes, colorful gardens, and beautiful lakes make"},{"startMs":564000,"endMs":566001,"text":"Golden Gate Park one of the wonders of the world."},{"startMs":570000,"endMs":582000,"text":"In a centrally located area of public buildings stands the DeYoung Museum, visited by more people than any museum in the country. A"},{"startMs":582000,"endMs":591001,"text":"fascinating collection of fish and reptiles from all over the world are displayed at the Steinhardt Aquarium. Within this black long conservatory is a veritable"},{"startMs":591001,"endMs":593001,"text":"paradise of rare tropical plants."},{"startMs":598000,"endMs":605000,"text":"The surrounding gardens offer an ever-changing display of"},{"startMs":605000,"endMs":607000,"text":"colorful seasonal blooms."},{"startMs":620000,"endMs":628001,"text":"In the exquisite Japanese tea garden, exotic pagodas create the atmosphere of the Far East."},{"startMs":643001,"endMs":648000,"text":"Blooming cherry blossoms enhance the beauty of moon bridges arching quiet lagoons."},{"startMs":657000,"endMs":660001,"text":"Scattered throughout the park are numerous lakes with their colorful water fowl."},{"startMs":663000,"endMs":670000,"text":"This lake is a mecca for hobbyists"},{"startMs":670000,"endMs":674001,"text":"who come to sail the miniature boats, while Stow Lake attracts those with a taste for rowing."},{"startMs":683001,"endMs":687000,"text":"Rising from the center of this lake is a rugged island with its plunging waterfall."},{"startMs":719001,"endMs":726001,"text":"Emerging from the park not far from where we entered, we continue our travels on the Great Highway, paralleling the Pacific Ocean."},{"startMs":746000,"endMs":750000,"text":"Of course, no tour of San Francisco is complete without a visit to the zoo."},{"startMs":760000,"endMs":762000,"text":"Could Darwin have been right?"},{"startMs":828000,"endMs":833000,"text":"For children of all ages, a ride on the miniature train is a thrilling experience."},{"startMs":900000,"endMs":904000,"text":"Between the recreational areas that border the ocean, we turn eastward toward the heart of the city."},{"startMs":910001,"endMs":920000,"text":"In the center of the city rise San Francisco's famous Twin Peaks."},{"startMs":927000,"endMs":932001,"text":"Reached by a spiraling road, the summit commands a spectacular view of the encircling city."},{"startMs":962000,"endMs":969001,"text":"Market Street, the main arterial through the downtown area, stretches like a broad ribbon from Twin Peaks to the Ferry Building."},{"startMs":993000,"endMs":1001000,"text":"The busy intersection of Powell and Market Streets in downtown San Francisco is located one of the terminals of the Powell Street cable car line."},{"startMs":1002000,"endMs":1009001,"text":"To reverse their direction, the cable cars are pushed onto the unique turntable and swung around manually by the motor man of the conductor."},{"startMs":1009001,"endMs":1012001,"text":"Much to the delight of the riders and spectators."},{"startMs":1016000,"endMs":1028000,"text":"These jaunty little relics of bygone days form a romantic link in San"},{"startMs":1028000,"endMs":1029001,"text":"Francisco's transportation system."},{"startMs":1051001,"endMs":1058000,"text":"Invented here in 1873 to travel over the steep hills, the cable cars have become a symbol of San Francisco."},{"startMs":1080000,"endMs":1084000,"text":"A top knob hill, we cross the California cable car line."},{"startMs":1085000,"endMs":1087001,"text":"The cars can be distinguished by their difference in color."},{"startMs":1090000,"endMs":1095001,"text":"On this route, we pass several of San Francisco's most renowned hotels."},{"startMs":1103001,"endMs":1109001,"text":"Aboard one of these venerable little cars, one enjoys a bell-rigging excursion up and down the San Francisco hills."},{"startMs":1128000,"endMs":1132001,"text":"Where the West meets the Orient, Grant Avenue, the heart of Chinatown."},{"startMs":1134000,"endMs":1138001,"text":"Along this narrow pagodas street, how is the exotic spirit of this oriental colony."},{"startMs":1139001,"endMs":1143000,"text":"The largest settlement of Chinese in the world outside of Asia."},{"startMs":1148000,"endMs":1153000,"text":"Bazaars and curioshops invite you to examine choices of jade, silk and rarentiques."},{"startMs":1178000,"endMs":1182000,"text":"There is no end to the interesting places one may visit in San Francisco."},{"startMs":1182001,"endMs":1185001,"text":"The Ferry Building, the churches and colleges."},{"startMs":1187001,"endMs":1192001,"text":"Or the tourists may prefer a leisurely drive along the many scenic boulevards."},{"startMs":1203000,"endMs":1210000,"text":"For the true adventurer, there is that final thrill. A ride down the world's most crooked streets."},{"startMs":1211001,"endMs":1213001,"text":"Eight hairpin turns in a single block."},{"startMs":1248000,"endMs":1251000,"text":"San Francisco, the cosmopolitan city."},{"startMs":1253000,"endMs":1254000,"text":"Queen of the Pacific."},{"startMs":1256001,"endMs":1258001,"text":"The city by the Golden Gate."},{"startMs":1262000,"endMs":1265000,"text":"Truly the city of many wonders."}]}